Victor: {
	DisplayName: Cyberware Doctor
	Bestiary: A cyberware doctor washed up on these shores, hauling enough cybernetic implants on his back to piece together an entire body. They say he can trade anyone's flesh for steel and electric current—as long as you can pay the price.
	TalkHint: Talk to Victor
	Name0: Victor

	TownNPCMood: {
		Content: All systems nominal. Like a freshly calibrated servo.
		NoHome: No clinic, no business. My operating table is still strapped to my back.
		FarFromHome: Too far from my clinic. None of my tools are within reach.
		LoveSpace: Spacious. Room for three operating tables. I like it.
		DislikeCrowded: Too many people. Forget about keeping anything sterile here.
		HateCrowded: Packed like this, someone will knock over my tray sooner or later.
		LoveBiome: I love {BiomeName}. Quiet, stable temperature - perfect for precision work.
		LikeBiome: "{BiomeName} is decent. My stock does not spoil here."
		DislikeBiome: The damp of {BiomeName} is crawling into my circuits. Terrible.
		HateBiome: "{BiomeName}? That place chews the finest chrome down to rust. Don't get me started."
		LoveNPC: "{NPCName} understands machines. A rare quality these days."
		LikeNPC: "{NPCName} is a decent neighbor, and a steady source of spare parts."
		DislikeNPC: "{NPCName} calls my surgery 'back-alley work'. Hmph. Results speak for themselves."
		HateNPC: Keep {NPCName} away from me. I'd rather not reassemble blast victims every other day.
		LikeNPC_Princess: Who could hate {NPCName}? Besides, her bone structure is of considerable research value.
		Princess_LovesNPC: I love {NPCName}! He always puts everyone back together good as new!
	}
}

TBUG: {
	DisplayName: Exploit Dealer
	Bestiary: The night Skeletron fell, the world tore open along a seam that never closed properly, and spat her out. She hit the ground hard; the first thing she asked after getting up was the local coin exchange rate. Now she runs a little shop, selling chips of origins best left unexplained.
	TalkHint: Talk to TBUG
	Name0: TBUG

	TownNPCMood: {
		Content: Running normally. No errors, no warnings. Almost boring.
		NoHome: No house. Strictly speaking, my current coordinates are an illegal value.
		FarFromHome: Too far from home. The signal attenuation is terrible.
		LoveSpace: All this space? Room for three monitors. I like it.
		DislikeCrowded: Too many people. Anyone could peek at my screen. Annoying.
		HateCrowded: Packed like this, someone will trip over my cables sooner or later.
		LoveBiome: "{BiomeName} is cool and stable. Smells like a server room."
		LikeBiome: "{BiomeName} is fine. Low temperatures are good for the hardware."
		DislikeBiome: The humidity alarm in {BiomeName} never stops.
		HateBiome: "{BiomeName}? My gear took seawater once. I still keep that repair bill."
		LoveNPC: "{NPCName} can talk wrenches and circuits both. No need to downclock around her."
		LikeNPC: "{NPCName} never asks where I came from, only whether I buy secondhand parts. Approved."
		DislikeNPC: "{NPCName} keeps trying to get me on his table and take me apart. I'm not broken. Don't fix me."
		HateNPC: "{NPCName}'s ledger is nastier than any virus. Keep him away from my shop."
		LikeNPC_Princess: "{NPCName}? Fine. Nobody manages to hate her, which is suspicious in itself."
		Princess_LovesNPC: I love {NPCName}! She knows so many things nobody else does!
	}
}
